
🚀 Amazon Devices Builder Tools for AI - Initialize Context
========================================================

DESCRIPTION:
  This tool installs (updates) the context document and sets up the MCP config
  for your AI agent to get insights for Amazon Devices App development.

  Two guidance modes are available:
    - Steering mode (default): installs a steering document into your workspace,
      which your AI agent picks up automatically in every session in that workspace.
    - Agent mode (--install-agent): installs adbt-dev, a dedicated, opt-in
      Amazon Devices agent that provides the same guidance but only when you
      explicitly invoke adbt-dev, with no always-on steering doc. See the
      --install-agent option below.

  In its default (steering) mode, this command will:
    1. Display available AI agents and their context file requirements
    2. Let you select your preferred AI agent from the supported list
    3. Update selected agent's MCP settings to configure the Amazon Devices Builder Tools MCP server
    4. Ask for context installation directory (defaults to current working directory)
    5. Handle existing context files by offering to merge or update content
    6. Create the appropriate context file in the correct location for your chosen AI agent
    7. Install skills (curated + Amazon Developers led community skills) to the agent's skills directory

USAGE:
  npx @amazon-devices/amazon-devices-buildertools-mcp@latest init-context [options]

OPTIONS:
  -a, --agent <type>               Target AI agent (cursor, cline, kiro, claude-code-cli, 
                                   github-copilot, other)
  -p, --context-document-path      Path to save context document
  -d, --skip-context-document      Skip context document installation (MCP config only)
  -m, --skip-mcp-config            Skip MCP configuration (context document only)
  -c, --clean                      Clean opposing artifacts before install (agent mode: delete
                                   steering; steering mode: delete agent file)
      --install-agent              Install adbt-dev, a dedicated Amazon Devices agent, for the
                                   selected host instead of the always-on steering doc (opt-in;
                                   invoke the agent explicitly to get ADBT guidance)
  -f, --force                      Skip all confirmation prompts and force overwrite existing configuration
  -h, --help                       Show this help message

EXAMPLES:
  # Interactive mode (default)
  npx @amazon-devices/amazon-devices-buildertools-mcp@latest init-context

  # Non-interactive with specific agent (steering mode)
  npx @amazon-devices/amazon-devices-buildertools-mcp@latest init-context --agent cursor --force
  npx @amazon-devices/amazon-devices-buildertools-mcp@latest init-context -a cursor -f

  # Agent mode: install the adbt-dev agent for the selected host (instead of the steering doc)
  npx @amazon-devices/amazon-devices-buildertools-mcp@latest init-context --agent kiro --install-agent

  # Agent mode: install the agent and hard-delete any existing steering doc
  npx @amazon-devices/amazon-devices-buildertools-mcp@latest init-context --agent kiro --force --install-agent --clean

  # Switch back to steering mode: remove the agent file before installing the steering doc
  npx @amazon-devices/amazon-devices-buildertools-mcp@latest init-context --agent kiro --force --clean

  # MCP config only (skip context document)
  npx @amazon-devices/amazon-devices-buildertools-mcp@latest init-context --agent cursor --skip-context-document
  npx @amazon-devices/amazon-devices-buildertools-mcp@latest init-context -a cursor -d

  # Context document only with custom path (skip MCP config)
  npx @amazon-devices/amazon-devices-buildertools-mcp@latest init-context --agent kiro --context-document-path ./docs --skip-mcp-config
  npx @amazon-devices/amazon-devices-buildertools-mcp@latest init-context -a kiro -p ./docs -m

  # Show help for init-context command
  npx @amazon-devices/amazon-devices-buildertools-mcp@latest init-context --help

SUPPORTED AI AGENTS:
  1. cursor                 - Cursor
  2. claude-code-cli        - Claude Code
  3. github-copilot         - GitHub Copilot
  4. kiro                   - Kiro
  5. cline                  - Cline
  6. opencode               - OpenCode
  7. codex                  - Codex
  8. gemini-cli             - Gemini CLI / Antigravity CLI
  9. other                  - Other/Custom Agent

For more information, visit:
  https://www.npmjs.com/package/@amazon-devices/amazon-devices-buildertools-mcp

